    "body": "### Problem\n\nI realised that many languages have syntax highlighting with the default colorscheme.\nHowever, there is no syntax highlighting in the case of ruby unless I change the colorscheme.\nIf I execute this command, for example, at least I get a bit of bold highlighting. \n```vim\nhighlight PreProc gui=bold\n```\nI reproduced it at the latest release.\n\nWould it be proper to create a pull request?\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n:colorscheme default\n:e script.rb\nInsert\n```\nclass Hey\n  def task(arg1)\n  end\nend\nvar1 = { sand: 1 }\nlist = [2, 3]\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nRuby syntax highlighting by default.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12.3\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, it works well\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nDebian 13 Linux/GNU\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nKonsole 25.04.2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nappimage",
